ERROR [open_webui.utils.hive_embed_attribution] hive (#1696): embedding endpoint 'http://127.0.0.1:9912' is not the Hive gateway, refusing to forward a signed-in user credential to it. This is either a misconfiguration or an attempt to harvest user sessions by rewriting the persistent RAG endpoint; the environment is the authority here, not Open WebUI config.
ERROR [open_webui.utils.hive_embed_attribution] hive (#1696): no upstream credential for user user-no-session, refusing to embed under the shared shim key; this spend would otherwise land on a platform account instead of on the customer
refused: hive (#1696): no signed-in user credential for this embedding call
request reached the upstream: False

Reading. Leg 1: the shim key stays on Authorization, which is what gates the
carrier at edge-api, and the searching user's own token rides on the carrier.
Leg 2 is the HIGH finding from the review, closed: the destination is Open
WebUI persistent config that any instance admin can rewrite, and on this shared
instance every tenant OWNER is an instance admin, so a repointed endpoint would
otherwise have collected one live session bearer per user who searched. The
module compares the destination against the ENVIRONMENT and refuses before a
credential is even resolved, so nothing reaches the attacker and nothing is
minted. Leg 3: a user with no resolvable session is refused rather than sent
under the shared key.
